REVYTECHCommander is a FreeBSD-native platform for running many LLM bots
as configuration (name, system prompt, allowed models, rate limits)
rather than binaries. A gateway serves HTTP/SSE with session cookies,
workers pull NATS JetStream jobs and call Ollama, Claude, Grok,
FreeGrok, MiniMax, or LiteLLM, and a conductor reconciles desired bot
state plus the transactional outbox.

HTTPS is terminated by Caddy (Let's Encrypt DNS-01). The service mesh is
WireGuard + Consul + Nomad + NATS mTLS, not Envoy. Postgres holds chat
state; Valkey holds sessions and rate limits.

WWW: https://github.com/revytechinc/REVYTECHCommander
